# Container image CVE exceptions.
# GENERATED by scripts/gen_trivyignore.py from security/accepted-risks.yml --
# do not hand-edit. Edit the registry and regenerate.
# Security acceptance standard (operator, 2026-10-08; shared with
# datawatch-app, dmz006/datawatch#197). See security/accepted-risks.yml's
# header for the schema, and scripts/check_accepted_risks.py for the lint.

# zlib1g -- CVE-2023-45853
# severity: critical; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full
# CVE-2023-45853 is an integer overflow in zlib's contrib MiniZip
# (zipOpenNewFileInZip4_64) when a caller passes an overlong filename, comment
# or extra field while WRITING a zip. It is not in inflate() (the earlier
# wording was wrong) and Debian ships MiniZip as separate libminizip packages,
# not in zlib1g. zlib1g stays installed only as an essential dependency of git,
# curl, libcurl4, openssh-client and tmux. grep of agent-base, agent-gemini,
# agent-aider and parent-full Dockerfiles finds no minizip/libminizip package;
# zip/unzip (Info-ZIP) bundle their own code and do not link MiniZip. datawatch
# Go sources use only the stdlib compress/gzip (server.go, api_gzip.go,
# main.go), which is pure Go and never calls libz. No MiniZip caller exists, so
# the vulnerable function is unreachable. zlib1g cannot be removed (essential).
# No fix available in Debian bookworm as of this migration; re-check each
# release cycle (BL398 Phase 1's live rescan baseline).
# TRACED: grep of docker/dockerfiles (agent-base, agent-gemini, agent-aider,
# parent-full) for minizip/zip tooling plus grep of internal/ and cmd/ Go
# sources for zlib/compress use; CVE description read
CVE-2023-45853

# libsqlite3-0 -- CVE-2025-7458
# severity: critical; images: agent-aider, agent-base, agent-gemini, parent-full
# CVE-2025-7458 is an integer overflow in SQLite core that needs
# attacker-supplied SQL text or a crafted database; The earlier claim that the
# gh CLI uses SQLite is wrong: gh is built from source in the ghbuilder stage
# with CGO_ENABLED=0 and is a statically linked Go ELF, so it links no
# libsqlite3. In agent-base the only installed package depending on libsqlite3-0
# is gpg (ldd confirms /usr/bin/gpg is the only binary linking it, via its TOFU
# trust database); git, apt, curl, tmux and openssh do not link it, and
# agent-base has no python3. Nothing in datawatch Go sources, scripts or
# entrypoints invokes gpg; gnupg is only used at image build time for the
# nodesource apt key. datawatch itself uses the pure-Go modernc.org/sqlite
# driver (internal/memory, websearch, council, docsindex), built CGO_ENABLED=0,
# so it never loads the system library. agent-aider adds python3 whose _sqlite3
# module links libsqlite3-0 (aider's diskcache and tags cache use fixed SQL, no
# FTS5, and no attacker-supplied SQL or FTS5 tables). agent-gemini adds only
# nodejs and gnupg. parent-full adds a headless JRE. No path reaches the
# vulnerable code with attacker input.
# No fix available in Debian bookworm as of this migration; re-check each
# release cycle (BL398 Phase 1's live rescan baseline).
# TRACED: docker run --network none on a built agent-base image: dpkg Depends
# scan for libsqlite3-0 and ldd over /usr/bin, git-core and /usr/local/bin;
# Dockerfile and Go/script grep for sqlite, gpg and python use
CVE-2025-7458

